Subject: Stagger the SIGCHLD fixture's sleeping children
Description: Peios runs Bash's upstream test suite as a build gate, and
 the trap8 fixture fails intermittently there because SIGCHLD signals from
 simultaneous child exits can coalesce. Staggering the children makes the
 gate deterministic without changing what it asserts.
Author: Peios maintainers <packaging@peios.org>
Origin: vendor, test fixture race fix
Forwarded: no

Concurrent equal-duration child exits make the SIGCHLD fixture race: standard
signals may coalesce, so fewer CHLD traps can run than the golden output
expects. Keep the same four children, job-control operations and expected
output, but separate the three sleep completions.

--- a/tests/trap8.sub
+++ b/tests/trap8.sub
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 wait

 sleep 1 &
-sleep 1 &
+sleep 2 &

-sleep 1
+sleep 3
 wait
